// control_plane.proto — DashCenter northbound mutating API.
//
// This is the operator-facing service that dashctl, the Web Console, and
// 3rd-party SDKs talk to. It is the ONLY surface that mutates desired state.
//
// Relationship to dashapi.v1 (southbound)
// ---------------------------------------
// dashapi.v1 is the *southbound* contract dashd uses to talk to each DPU agent
// (dash-sim, dash-redis-adapter, real DPUs). dashcenter.v1 (this file) is the
// *northbound* contract operators use to talk to dashd. dashd is responsible
// for translating northbound intent into per-DPU dashapi.v1 calls via its
// placement function and 5-stage write pipeline:
//
//     Receive → Validate → Stage(pending:txn_id) → Dispatch → Commit(MULTI/EXEC)
//
// Multi-tenancy
// -------------
// Every spec message carries a `namespace` field. Namespace boundaries are
// enforced at validation time; cross-namespace references (e.g. an ENI in
// namespace "team-a" pointing at a VNET in namespace "shared") are rejected
// unless the target namespace explicitly exports the object (out of scope for
// this file — handled by dashd RBAC config).
//
// Generations & optimistic concurrency
// ------------------------------------
// Every Put* carries an optional `expected_generation`. If non-zero, dashd
// returns FAILED_PRECONDITION when the current stored generation differs.
// Returned Ack messages always include the new generation in `txn_id` metadata
// (the txn_id is the canonical handle for follow-up queries).
//
// Streaming
// ---------
// ApplyBatch is a *client-streaming* RPC: the client streams PolicyObject
// messages, the server commits them as a single Stage→Dispatch→Commit
// transaction, and returns one terminal BatchAck. SimulateApply is unary but
// returns a synthesised SimulateApplyResult without mutating anything.

